################ WHAT THE THREE RUNS ESTABLISH

RUN 1  born-RED. With one real hollow bank's grandfather line removed —
       `pass3/dist-head`, 2 files, `_headers` + `_redirects`, the exact BC5-G2 shape —
       the gate reds with one breach, names the rule (`dist-loose`), names the path, and
       prints the two ways out. EXIT 1. The rule bites the thing it was written for.

RUN 2  the line restored (verified by diff against the pre-probe copy: identical), the
       gate is GREEN across the whole estate: 29 directory banks, 0 archives, 29 dist
       pins, PASS. 22/22 self-test cases, up from 9.

RUN 3  exit honesty, probed adversarially: self-test GREEN and estate RED in one
       invocation. `--self-test` printed 22/22 PASS and the process still exited 1 on the
       audit's verdict. The self-test proves the instrument; it does not stand in for the
       audit, and it cannot swallow a breach. Source restored byte-identical afterwards.

The 13 new self-test cases cover every arm of rule 4 in both directions: a new hollow bank
reds; a FULL loose bank reds too (the rule is the FORM, not the payload); a TESTIMONY.md
that says the words exempts; one that does not say them buys nothing; an archive without a
manifest reds; an archive with a non-empty sibling md5 passes; an EMPTY manifest is not a
manifest; a pin exempts at its count and reds above it; a stale pin is reported; `distillate/`
is not a dist bank; build output nested inside a bank is not a second bank; and an estate with
no bank at all reds nowhere (the anti-vacuity control).
